# A submodule does NOT inherit the superproject's .gitattributes — attributes are per-repository. This file
# is the one that actually protects the game data, so it deliberately repeats the parent's rules rather than
# assuming them.
#
# The stakes here are higher than in the code repo: data/ is ~1750 binary terrain files plus the CSV/Lua
# content registry, authored on Windows and checked out on a Linux host.

* text=auto eol=lf

# ---- content registry (read as text by Content.Load / MoonSharp) ----
*.csv       text eol=lf
*.lua       text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf

# ---- terrain and client tables (read as raw bytes) ----
# A CRLF substitution inside one of these does not fail — it silently corrupts collision or a lookup table.
*.map       binary
*.cmp       binary
*.tbl       binary
*.epf       binary
*.pal       binary
*.frm       binary
*.db        binary
